Practical 3
Creating Applications with Data (CRUD)
CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) forms the
foundational architecture for managing persistent
data records in enterprise web applications. In
ASP.NET Core, these four basic data-handling
operations map directly to specialized standard
HTTP architectural protocols, domain models, and
Entity Framework (EF) Core state-tracking
mechanisms.
Entity Framework (EF) Core is Microsoft's
lightweight, open-source, and cross-platform ObjectRelational Mapper (ORM). It enables developers to
interact with relational and NoSQL databases using
C# objects and LINQ, eliminating the need to write
and maintain manual data-access code or raw SQL
queries.
Student Management System
This practical demonstrates how to create a CRUD (Create, Read,
Update, Delete) application using:
 ASP.NET MVC 5
 .NET Framework 4.7.2
 Entity Framework 6
 SQL Server LocalDB
 Visual Studio 2019
Aim
To create a Student Management System that allows users to:
1. Add a new student.
2. Display student records.
3. Edit student information.
4. Delete student records.
